WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:04.510 --> 00:08.250
Satoshi has finally reached the finals of the Kalos League.

00:09.290 --> 00:12.940
His opponent is the tough Alan!

00:20.240 --> 00:22.480
Thunderbolt is super effective!

00:23.040 --> 00:24.790
Lizardon withstood the attack!

00:25.370 --> 00:27.000
Pikachu, Quick Attack!

00:29.500 --> 00:30.370
Flamethrower!

00:36.390 --> 00:36.980
Pikachu!

00:37.520 --> 00:38.930
Whoa! Pikachu can't move!

00:40.630 --> 00:42.380
I wonder if Pikachu is all right.

00:43.510 --> 00:45.650
It's still suffering from the damage it sustained in previous battles.

00:46.240 --> 00:47.360
Fly into the air, Lizardon!

00:49.030 --> 00:50.400
Stand, Pikachu!

00:52.680 --> 00:53.400
Flamethrower!

00:56.340 --> 00:57.440
Iron Tail!

00:57.590 --> 00:58.600
Whip up some sand!

01:04.660 --> 01:05.680
I've got to hand it to you.

01:06.140 --> 01:07.000
Dragon Claw!

01:07.360 --> 01:08.010
Iron Tail!

01:14.290 --> 01:15.300
Pikachu!

01:18.090 --> 01:19.630
Pikachu is unable to battle!

01:20.040 --> 01:21.060
Lizardon wins!

01:21.920 --> 01:23.450
Pikachu is defeated!

01:23.780 --> 01:25.230
With that, the score has once again been evened!

01:25.540 --> 01:27.270
They now have two Pokémon left each!

01:27.990 --> 01:29.460
Pikachu, are you all right?

01:31.430 --> 01:32.030
Thank you.

01:32.430 --> 01:33.270
You did your best.

01:34.080 --> 01:35.020
Leave the rest to us.

01:40.850 --> 01:42.200
The match has just begun.

01:46.240 --> 01:52.000
Kalos League Victory!
Satoshi's Ultimate Match!!

01:53.010 --> 02:02.920
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:53.010 --> 02:02.920
Z

01:53.270 --> 01:55.330
The Pokémon League finals are a fierce fight!

01:56.630 --> 02:00.710
Satoshi's Pikachu stood no chance against Alan's Lizardon.

01:59.200 --> 02:01.610
Geez... What's Pikachu doing?

02:01.080 --> 02:02.970
They have now defeated four Pokémon each.

02:01.610 --> 02:03.550
It trampled all over our feelings.

02:03.550 --> 02:06.550
Now, both of them only have two Pokémon left!

02:04.290 --> 02:06.550
Uh... Since when are you rooting for the brat boy?

02:07.340 --> 02:09.340
We don't like it either!

02:09.680 --> 02:11.700
We're talking about the brat boy, our old nemesis!

02:11.970 --> 02:14.350
He's not gonna lose to that guy!

02:17.520 --> 02:19.640
Let's all root for the brat boy!

02:20.100 --> 02:21.070
Yeah!

02:21.870 --> 02:25.300
Aw... Pikachu lost.

02:26.820 --> 02:29.210
Alan has Lizardon and Kirikizan left...

02:30.200 --> 02:33.820
However, none of Alan's Pokémon are at full health.

02:34.770 --> 02:38.600
Satoshi, on the other hand, has nothing <i>but</i> Pokémon that are at full health!

02:39.230 --> 02:40.990
If you look at it like that, he does have the advantage!

02:41.630 --> 02:42.850
Yeah, it'll be fine.

02:43.550 --> 02:45.050
Seeing Satoshi smile like that...

02:45.610 --> 02:46.970
...makes me sure of it.

02:52.070 --> 02:53.540
Do your best, Alan.

02:54.070 --> 02:55.810
Numelgon, I choose you!

02:59.860 --> 03:00.800
Return, Lizardon.

03:02.060 --> 03:04.780
Alan has now recalled Lizardon.

03:07.370 --> 03:08.690
Go, Kirikizan!

03:12.840 --> 03:17.160
Satoshi has chosen Numelgon, while Alain has sent out Kirikizan!

03:17.960 --> 03:19.740
First, let's change this to your favorite battlefield.

03:20.520 --> 03:21.540
Rain Dance!

03:26.850 --> 03:29.110
Numelgon has made it rain!

03:29.560 --> 03:30.810
Ice Beam!

03:32.970 --> 03:34.430
Dodge and use Iron Head!

03:36.990 --> 03:37.450
Block it!

03:40.490 --> 03:41.360
Fling it, Numelgon!

03:44.850 --> 03:45.860
Dragon Pulse!

03:48.590 --> 03:49.360
Focus Blast!

03:56.230 --> 03:57.080
Iron Head!

03:59.110 --> 03:59.400
Bide!

04:03.440 --> 04:03.980
Numelgon!

04:04.300 --> 04:04.990
Are you all right?

04:06.980 --> 04:07.670
Focus Blast!

04:13.310 --> 04:16.010
Numelgon keeps on enduring attacks!

04:16.320 --> 04:19.780
Will Satoshi's strategy be hit or miss?

04:20.900 --> 04:21.430
Go around it!

04:21.790 --> 04:22.430
Use Iron Head!

04:27.450 --> 04:27.740
Now!

04:35.470 --> 04:36.830
Are you all right, Kirikizan?

04:37.800 --> 04:40.060
Satoshi counterattacks!

04:40.190 --> 04:42.920
Numelgon has overpowered Kirikizan!

04:45.820 --> 04:49.450
Really though, Numelgon did a great job withstanding those attacks.

04:50.060 --> 04:52.010
They're having an interesting battle.

04:53.150 --> 04:55.410
I would've liked to watch it in the stadium as well.

04:56.430 --> 04:56.810
Citroid!

04:57.420 --> 04:59.130
I wanted to see it, too.

05:00.090 --> 05:01.070
Iron Head!

05:09.470 --> 05:10.070
Numelgon!

05:10.630 --> 05:13.090
That's a lot of damage! Numelgon's in trouble!

05:13.450 --> 05:14.450
Guillotine!

05:16.710 --> 05:18.350
Numelgon, Dragon Pulse!

05:36.240 --> 05:37.820
Numelgon is unable to battle!

05:38.650 --> 05:39.940
Kirikizan wins!

05:40.610 --> 05:43.780
Kirikizan has defeated Numelgon!

05:44.640 --> 05:46.440
Numelgon lost...

05:46.590 --> 05:47.460
Just one left...

05:48.050 --> 05:49.990
Hey... He has his back against the wall now.

05:51.960 --> 05:52.590
Satoshi...

05:54.870 --> 05:55.510
Numelgon...

05:55.960 --> 05:56.570
Thank you.

05:58.750 --> 05:59.810
I'll finish this with you.

06:00.400 --> 06:01.840
I'm counting on you, Gekkouga!

06:07.780 --> 06:10.170
Satoshi has sent out Gekkouga.

06:10.690 --> 06:13.500
This is his last Pokémon.

06:14.020 --> 06:17.790
The moment it is defeated, Alan will have won the league!

06:15.180 --> 06:18.980
Oh come on! Talking about Gekkouga being defeated like that just brings bad luck.

06:19.910 --> 06:20.910
It'll be fine.

06:21.160 --> 06:25.230
The more the brat boy is in trouble, the more he shows his latent power.

06:25.230 --> 06:27.550
Yeah. After all, we're the ones...

06:27.550 --> 06:28.980
...who made the brat boy strong!

06:32.910 --> 06:33.610
Kirikizan,

06:34.070 --> 06:35.550
Put all your energies into this!

06:38.140 --> 06:39.400
Let's do this, Gekkouga!

06:41.520 --> 06:42.510
Iron Head!

06:45.150 --> 06:45.670
Double Team!

06:50.030 --> 06:50.670
Water Shuriken!

07:02.240 --> 07:02.730
Kirikizan!

07:05.840 --> 07:07.190
Kirikizan is unable to battle!

07:08.010 --> 07:09.030
Gekkouga wins!

07:09.790 --> 07:10.700
All right!

07:11.990 --> 07:12.860
He did it!

07:15.300 --> 07:16.610
I see! It's the rain!

07:17.180 --> 07:18.430
Huh? What do you mean?

07:19.020 --> 07:21.710
Rain makes Water type moves more powerful.

07:22.230 --> 07:26.030
Numelgon's Rain Dance is now assisting Gekkouga.

07:27.450 --> 07:29.120
An assist from Numelgon...

07:29.550 --> 07:30.940
That was a victory won by everyone.

07:31.970 --> 07:32.470
Come out,

07:32.890 --> 07:33.610
Lizardon!

07:39.630 --> 07:41.420
Lizardon makes its appearance!

07:41.870 --> 07:43.760
Both competitors are down to their last Pokémon.

07:44.270 --> 07:46.430
This battle will decide everything!

07:51.310 --> 07:53.950
Lizardon, it's time for our long-awaited battle with Gekkouga.

07:54.780 --> 07:55.840
Let's enjoy this till the end.

07:58.890 --> 07:59.550
Gekkouga,

08:00.060 --> 08:01.680
this is a worthy opponent for you.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.170
Let's show them what we're like at our best!

08:05.370 --> 08:06.490
Run, Gekkouga!

08:07.920 --> 08:09.100
Fly into the air, Lizardon!

08:11.600 --> 08:12.690
Flamethrower!

08:14.350 --> 08:15.020
Dodge!

08:17.610 --> 08:19.000
Gekkouga, Cut!

08:23.390 --> 08:24.910
Cut hit its mark!

08:25.120 --> 08:26.780
That was definitely effective!

08:29.430 --> 08:31.660
Oh, now the rain has stopped!

08:31.660 --> 08:33.940
How will that change the course of events?

08:34.560 --> 08:37.220
So now the effect of Numelgon's Rain Dance is gone.

08:37.630 --> 08:40.150
Still, Gekkouga has the type advantage.

08:40.740 --> 08:41.260
Don't worry.

08:41.750 --> 08:43.220
Satoshi will win for sure.

08:44.230 --> 08:45.290
Let's go, Gekkouga!

08:47.240 --> 08:47.730
Alan...

08:48.480 --> 08:49.050
I...

08:49.780 --> 08:50.950
...<i>We</i> won't lose.

08:52.140 --> 08:53.530
Let's fight with our full power!

08:55.790 --> 08:56.570
Gekkouga!

09:11.680 --> 09:13.470
Here comes Satoshi Gekkouga!

09:15.190 --> 09:16.060
Marvelous!

09:19.240 --> 09:20.440
There it is!

09:22.630 --> 09:23.530
Thank you, Satoshi.

09:24.210 --> 09:25.950
I've been waiting for you to show that full power of yours.

09:26.640 --> 09:29.270
Take me to even higher stages!

09:30.300 --> 09:30.900
All right,

09:31.450 --> 09:32.370
this is the end.

09:33.480 --> 09:34.170
Lizardon!

09:34.340 --> 09:35.570
Respond to my heart,

09:36.110 --> 09:37.040
Key Stone!

09:37.480 --> 09:38.670
Surpass evolution!

09:38.900 --> 09:40.080
Mega evolve!

09:57.000 --> 09:58.020
Please, Lizardon...

09:58.540 --> 10:00.030
Make Alan win.

10:00.570 --> 10:03.320
Alan's Lizardon has mega evolved!

10:03.630 --> 10:08.210
It's the final round of the ultimate match of the Kalos League!

10:11.050 --> 10:11.990
Pokémon Quiz.

10:12.380 --> 10:13.090
The answer is...?

10:15.040 --> 10:24.990
Coming up next:

10:15.040 --> 10:20.020
The fateful last battle!

10:16.010 --> 10:20.700
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

10:20.050 --> 10:24.990
Will Satoshi win the league!?

10:31.810 --> 10:32.900
Run, Gekkouga!

10:36.720 --> 10:37.770
Double Team!

10:39.410 --> 10:40.770
Mow them down with Flamethrower!

10:44.010 --> 10:45.210
Water Shuriken!

10:49.470 --> 10:50.780
Dragon Claw!

10:54.750 --> 10:55.750
Aerial Ace!

10:56.280 --> 10:57.140
Dragon Claw!

11:10.520 --> 11:11.300
Flamethrower!

11:14.260 --> 11:15.220
Use Cut!

11:21.020 --> 11:22.350
Blast Burn!

11:27.340 --> 11:29.650
Plunge a Water Shuriken into the ground!

11:35.840 --> 11:38.500
It used Water Shuriken to block Blast Burn!

11:38.730 --> 11:41.160
I have never seen a fight like this before!

11:41.450 --> 11:42.470
Aerial Ace!

11:48.350 --> 11:49.710
Go, go, Satoshi!

11:49.710 --> 11:51.240
Go, go, Gekkouga!

11:52.530 --> 11:53.720
Are you all right, Lizardon?

11:59.000 --> 12:01.710
Alan is enjoying his battle with Satoshi.

12:07.290 --> 12:07.860
Satoshi...

12:08.810 --> 12:09.990
Thanks to you,

12:10.840 --> 12:12.120
I'm having a lot of fun right now.

12:13.790 --> 12:15.540
I'm grateful to you for making me...

12:16.150 --> 12:16.600
...feel this way.

12:17.720 --> 12:18.240
Thank you.

12:19.600 --> 12:19.950
But...

12:21.960 --> 12:23.600
...I have to be the strongest.

12:24.540 --> 12:26.030
I can't lose to anyone anymore!

12:26.790 --> 12:27.420
Lizardon,

12:27.970 --> 12:29.080
Dragon Claw!

12:36.520 --> 12:37.800
Its power is amazing.

12:38.190 --> 12:39.560
It still has so much strength...

12:43.130 --> 12:43.660
I'm having...

12:44.450 --> 12:46.540
...a lot of fun too, being able to fight...

12:46.970 --> 12:48.180
...a strong Trainer like you, Alain.

12:49.250 --> 12:50.430
But this is the end.

12:51.540 --> 12:53.620
No hard feelings, whatever the outcome, Alan.

12:54.270 --> 12:54.980
Take this!

12:55.240 --> 12:57.280
This is the full power of every one of us combined!

12:57.630 --> 12:59.190
Gekkouga, Cut!

13:01.880 --> 13:03.210
Lizardon, Dragon Claw!

13:17.040 --> 13:17.890
Water Shuriken!

13:17.040 --> 13:17.890
Thunder Punch!

13:23.100 --> 13:25.700
It used Water Shuriken to block Thunder Punch!

13:25.950 --> 13:27.700
What a struggle!

13:37.560 --> 13:38.430
Let's go, Alan!

13:38.710 --> 13:39.620
Water Shuriken!

13:46.420 --> 13:47.760
Blast Burn!

14:27.460 --> 14:28.800
Gekkouga is unable to battle.

14:29.150 --> 14:31.320
Therefore, the winner is Alan!

14:33.550 --> 14:35.410
It's decided!

14:35.650 --> 14:39.240
The one who won the continuous fierce fights of the Kalos League finals...

14:39.560 --> 14:41.680
...is Alan!

14:50.700 --> 14:51.630
He's so strong...

14:53.850 --> 14:54.840
He lost.

14:56.190 --> 14:57.360
Too bad.

14:57.870 --> 14:59.490
He was so close.

15:00.030 --> 15:01.490
But it was a good fight.

15:01.750 --> 15:02.080
Yes.

15:02.910 --> 15:04.750
That battle was so like Satoshi.

15:05.360 --> 15:06.710
Satoshi is smiling.

15:07.560 --> 15:11.710
I'm sure he's satisfied with the battle since he gave it all he got.

15:13.290 --> 15:14.820
You did great, Gekkouga.

15:16.630 --> 15:17.700
Don't apologize.

15:18.600 --> 15:20.760
I'm so grateful to you guys.

15:23.160 --> 15:23.630
Satoshi...

15:24.840 --> 15:25.270
Thank you.

15:26.180 --> 15:27.030
Likewise.

15:27.430 --> 15:29.650
Thank you very much for the fun battle.

15:38.440 --> 15:40.910
There is no longer a winner or a loser here.

15:41.590 --> 15:46.410
What we see here is nothing but the refreshing sight of two competitors who just finished their battle.

15:49.070 --> 15:51.820
I'm extremely moved right now!

15:51.820 --> 15:54.160
This is what Pokémon battles are about!

15:54.160 --> 15:56.200
I don't care about getting their Pokémon any more!

15:56.200 --> 15:58.210
I'm drunk on emotions right now!

16:01.740 --> 16:04.060
Good work, Alan. I'm so happy for you.

16:08.130 --> 16:08.430
Alan,

16:09.300 --> 16:12.190
has this made you find the answer you were looking for?

16:13.630 --> 16:17.110
Satoshi, it was a really great and impressive battle.

16:17.950 --> 16:20.360
I'm sorry I was unable to meet your expectations.

16:21.080 --> 16:25.730
You should not be. We all know you and your Pokémon did your best.

16:26.340 --> 16:28.050
Alan really was strong.

16:28.560 --> 16:30.890
Lizardon's tenacity was really impressive.

16:31.350 --> 16:34.530
I've got to meet a lot more Trainers and Pokémon...

16:34.820 --> 16:35.420
...and...

16:35.930 --> 16:37.730
...become a lot stronger.

16:38.070 --> 16:39.110
Right, Pikachu?

16:46.670 --> 16:48.170
Through this battle, Satoshi and his Pokémon...

16:49.630 --> 16:51.430
...made us grow.

16:53.300 --> 16:53.720
Let's go...

16:54.900 --> 16:56.630
...collect Mega Evolution energy again.

16:57.570 --> 16:58.240
We need just a bit more.

17:14.610 --> 17:16.120
All preparations are complete.

17:16.990 --> 17:17.930
We will start now.

17:35.290 --> 17:35.730
Alan...

17:37.490 --> 17:45.400
I laud you for being a Trainer that raised his Pokémon well, formed a strong bond with them, and displayed unprecedented strength.

17:45.960 --> 17:46.570
Congratulations.

17:47.070 --> 17:48.030
Thank you very much.

17:53.530 --> 17:54.030
Alan.

17:55.830 --> 17:56.630
Congratulations!

17:59.820 --> 18:01.180
Congratulations, Alan!

18:01.490 --> 18:03.900
This is great. This is really great.

18:04.300 --> 18:05.440
Don't you agree, Fleur-de-l...

18:07.580 --> 18:08.320
Fleur-de-lis-san?

18:11.630 --> 18:13.700
This is precisely why humans...

18:14.020 --> 18:15.630
Why humans...

18:20.230 --> 18:21.180
Fleur-de-lis-sama...

18:21.580 --> 18:24.180
We will finally see the results of our research.

18:26.850 --> 18:27.530
Zygarde!

18:28.380 --> 18:31.280
Show me your power!

18:31.770 --> 18:33.680
Humans are foolish.

18:34.060 --> 18:34.870
Disappear!

18:35.500 --> 18:37.220
The foolish creatures throughout this world...

18:37.610 --> 18:39.500
...shall all be gone!

18:53.200 --> 18:53.980
The curtain rises...

18:54.680 --> 18:56.940
...for my greatest show!

19:31.200 --> 19:32.430
What on earth...?

19:34.730 --> 19:37.830
Everything in this world will be reborn...

19:38.960 --> 19:40.350
...into a beautiful world.

19:48.630 --> 19:49.510
What's that?

19:49.870 --> 19:51.120
What's going on?

19:54.700 --> 19:55.120
What?

19:59.540 --> 20:00.180
Squishy!

20:00.400 --> 20:01.090
Wait!

20:02.020 --> 20:03.620
Eureka, where are you going?

20:05.210 --> 20:08.670
A disaster has suddenly befallen the Kalos League.

20:09.520 --> 20:10.940
What is Zygarde's power?

20:11.560 --> 20:14.460
And what is Fleur-de-lis' motive?

20:26.040 --> 20:28.250
The passionate and exciting points of the Pokémon movie!

20:28.510 --> 20:29.550
Get blown away!

20:30.940 --> 21:21.020
The blockbuster is
currently in theaters!

20:31.380 --> 20:35.580
Your soul will be the stronghold that will protect the people of this country.

20:36.110 --> 20:38.910
In the end, Volcanion's special friend, Magearna,

20:39.420 --> 20:40.330
Mega Wave!

20:40.670 --> 20:41.860
I ain't gonna let ya get away with this!

20:42.600 --> 20:47.330
What I need to fulfill my ideals is not Magearna, just the Soul Heart!

20:47.510 --> 20:50.250
...ends up falling into Jarvis' evil clutches!

20:50.740 --> 20:52.310
The sealed power...

20:52.780 --> 20:54.500
...now reawakens!

20:55.050 --> 20:55.600
So that's...

20:56.340 --> 20:57.280
...the Flying Fortress.

20:57.490 --> 21:02.250
The Soul Heart revives an ancient weapon and the world falls into a crisis!

21:02.250 --> 21:03.090
That flower field...

21:04.020 --> 21:06.870
...is where I first met Magearna.

21:07.520 --> 21:11.890
Will Volcanion be able to save Magearna... and the whole world?

21:12.330 --> 21:13.660
Volcanion!

21:14.010 --> 21:14.870
Magearna...

21:15.910 --> 21:16.930
I'm sorry.

21:17.400 --> 21:20.340
Watch the moving conclusion in theaters!

21:21.020 --> 21:26.010
Sunday August 21st at 8am!

21:21.820 --> 21:23.800
Abareru-kun does a prank kiss!

21:21.840 --> 21:23.300
<i>All</i> my dreams...

21:24.060 --> 21:25.530
Ew!

21:24.240 --> 21:25.530
On Sunday at 8am!

21:28.150 --> 21:30.060
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.260 --> 21:31.340
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.860 --> 21:35.730
Miare City was attacked by a sudden outbreak of plants!

21:35.730 --> 21:37.780
Look at the top of the Prism Tower!

21:38.030 --> 21:38.510
What's that?

21:38.940 --> 21:40.460
Squishy is heading over there!

21:40.710 --> 21:41.650
What? Really?

21:41.910 --> 21:43.580
Yeah. Eureka just knows!

21:43.580 --> 21:45.230
Wait a second, Eureka! That is dangerous!

21:45.750 --> 21:48.150
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:48.560 --> 21:52.060
The Flare Gang Attacks! The Zygarde at the Prism Tower!!

21:52.470 --> 21:55.960
Next Time

21:52.470 --> 21:55.960
The Flare Gang Attacks!
The Zygarde at the Prism Tower!!

21:52.740 --> 21:53.630
Everyone,

21:53.900 --> 21:54.740
get Pokémon!

21:56.000 --> 22:06.020
Next episode:

21:56.000 --> 22:00.970
Danger befalls Miare City!

21:56.720 --> 22:01.310
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:00.970 --> 22:06.020
The Flare Gang finally makes its move
